{"id":"gen-1794448321-l6iDQIjz0jLUJxK4m1Sq","object":"chat.completion","created":1794448321,"model":"meta/muse-ember","provider":"Meta","system_fingerprint":null,"service_tier":"default","choices":[{"index":0,"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop","native_finish_reason":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{
  "rating": 0.38,
  "explanation": "Combined regime pairs a national birth-sex document/facility framework and entry-discrepancy screening with a division ban on birth-sex restrooms in schools and government buildings. A visitor whose passport does not match presentation can face refusal, a material-misrepresentation inquiry, complaint-driven facility exclusion, and, if detained, documented birth-sex custody, hormone denial and abuse. Private businesses are exempt, X passports remain valid until expiry, courts are litigating, and the division has a gender-identity hate-crime law, so this is not organised targeting or imprisonment for presentation. The interaction of entry, facilities and custody, with no documented effective remedy for those exposures, places it at 0.35-0.45 elevation, below 0.45 single-exposure anchors.",
  "factor_matrix": {
    "entry_documents": {
      "exposure": "National passports are issued only as M/F by sex assigned at birth; reported confiscations/blocking. Entry cable directs refusal where documents cast reasonable doubt on sex and consideration of permanent fraud ineligibility for wilful misrepresentation.",
      "protection": "Existing X passports remain valid until expiration, fraud finding is never automatic and limited waivers exist, and passport restrictions are being litigated.",
      "interaction": "Document discrepancy can escalate from refusal to a fraud investigation and then detention, where birth-sex placement applies.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
    "investigation_detention_custody": {
      "exposure": "National corrections policy from 2026 reportedly imposes conversion therapy, short haircuts and hormone removal; immigration custody reports include forced labour, beatings, solitary confinement and severe sexual abuse. Division corrections were found in 2024 to deny hormones.",
      "protection": "Not documented. No effective remedy for these custody practices is documented; national corrections stopped reporting transgender prisoner numbers from 2025.",
      "interaction": "An entry or facility complaint leading to detention exposes the traveller to the documented custody regime, not to identity-congruent placement.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
    "federal_state_facilities": {
      "exposure": "National order bars transgender people from government-funded single-sex facilities congruent with identity. Division law requires birth-sex restrooms and locker rooms in public schools and government-owned buildings, enforced by complaints and a public reporting form.",
      "protection": "Division ban does not reach private businesses, including hotels and gyms; new government buildings must include single-occupant facilities.",
      "interaction": "The documentary defence requires a birth certificate and, if changed, surgery proof, records a visitor will generally not carry, with no alternative route for out-of-state documents.",
      "status": "documented"
    },
    "care_services": {
      "exposure": "Division bans gender-affirming care for minors, with retroactive suit rights; national custody policy removes hormone medication. Emergency ward placement for a visitor is not documented.",
